      ],
      "prompt": "Given that $y=-11\\operatorname{ln}x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-11\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =-11\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =-11\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{11}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "absent_attributes": []
    },
